   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Received from <name type="person" key="weav76">Harriet Weaver</name> the sum of £200 (two hundred pounds str) advance of royalties on <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">the Paris edition</seg> of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">
                            <hi rend="underline">Ulysses</hi>
                        </name>.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <dateline>                                                       	<name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name> <date when="1921-05-02">2 May 1921</date>
                        </dateline>
                        <signed>                                                                    	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">JJ sent this receipt to Harriet Weaver as an enclosure to his <rs type="letter" key="L_68763">letter of 2 May 1921</rs> (<name type="work">LI</name> 164-65). The receipt was omitted from the published text.</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Weaver’s “advance” was actually a gift, since royalties on the Paris edition were paid to JJ by Sylvia Beach.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
